    "detailed_description": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >About</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tired of city building where you have to micromanage everything?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pico Topia is a simple and relaxing citybuilder where you place tiny tiles, combine them to collect points and unlock new tiles.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Combining tiles will either increase or reduce your points. If you lose too many points, the game ends.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Leveling up</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you gain enough points, you will level up and unlock new islands that you can the place in your world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unlocking an island also gives you the chance to add it to your starter cards.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Starter Cards</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you beat your high score of your previous world, you will be able to unlock a starter card.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The first three cards you start a world with will be chosen from your starter card collection, making every start to a new world different.</p>",
    "about_the_game": "<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >About</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><strong>Tired of city building where you have to micromanage everything?</strong></p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Pico Topia is a simple and relaxing citybuilder where you place tiny tiles, combine them to collect points and unlock new tiles.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Combining tiles will either increase or reduce your points. If you lose too many points, the game ends.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Leveling up</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >If you gain enough points, you will level up and unlock new islands that you can the place in your world.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >Unlocking an island also gives you the chance to add it to your starter cards.</p><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" >Starter Cards</h2><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >When you beat your high score of your previous world, you will be able to unlock a starter card.</p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" >The first three cards you start a world with will be chosen from your starter card collection, making every start to a new world different.</p>",
